import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioFixStretch
import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRulesAllSheet
import Googology.Trans.BMS.TrioRow3480

/-!
# Fix S against the sheet, and its own checks

`TrioFixStretch.lean` is a patch (Fix S) on top of `TrioRulesAll.lean` (rules 1–10 of
[koteitan/trio](https://github.com/koteitan/trio) with Fixes A–E and N).  It fixes the
stretch from `β+Ω_2` to `β·2`, `β = Ω_ω·Ω` ([TRIO-ROW-3480.md](TRIO-ROW-3480.md)).
This file re-runs every check of `TrioRulesAllSheet.lean` for the patched rules
(`sOf`, `trioRuleMatrixOfS` in place of `allOf`, `trioRuleMatrixOfAll`), then adds
Fix S's own checks (Part 8).

* **The sheet** ([`tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv`](https://github.com/koteitan/trio/blob/main/tools/omega_alpha_rows.tsv)):
  every guard of Parts 1–4 of `TrioRulesAllSheet.lean` holds with the patched rules,
  except the guard of row 3480, which changes on purpose: the row now gets `c2`.  On
  the 822 labels (813 rows, 9 corrected `L` labels) Fix S changes exactly three labels
  (`stretch3`): rows 3480 `β+Ω_3` (`c2`), 3481 `β+Ω_ω` (`lM`) and 3482 `β·2` (`b1`).
  Rows 3481 and 3482 are two of the 28 rows whose sheet matrix is not standard; the new
  matrices are standard (yaBMS `bms -s`; `c2` is proved standard in `TrioRow3480.lean`).
* **The order checks**: the 783 chosen matrices (306,153 pairs), the 784 with the
  printed label of row 3552 (306,936 pairs), and the 785 with row 3480 (`c2`, 307,720
  pairs): 0 disagreements.
* **The fixes' own guards** (Fixes A–E and N, Parts 2–4) and the interaction checks
  (Parts 5–6) hold unchanged, with the three labels of `stretch3` as the only new
  difference.  Part 7: on the 1,225 labels, the patched step differs from rules
  1–10's on 260 sums (257 before: the three labels of `stretch3`).
* **Part 8, Fix S**: the matrices TRIO-ROW-3480.md asks for; 69 labels from `β` to
  `β·ω`, in order (0 disagreements; 307 before) and against the 785 (0); BMS
  expansion (`(β+Ω_ω)[n] = β+Ω_{n+2}`, `(β·ω)[n] = β·(n+1)`, …); 525 labels on 21
  bases (disagreements 654 → 537, never more on any base).  All 69 matrices of the
  family are standard (yaBMS `bms -s`, outside Lean; 54 of them were not).

All of it is `#guard`s: a calibration, not a theorem.
-/

